{"ts":"2026-08-05T18:51:51.003Z","type":"quest-declared","sealed":{"doneWhen":{"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/durable-withdrawal-cleanup-intent-v2.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["withdrawal-intent-durable-across-teardown","lease-expiry-fallback-explicit","reaper-drives-status-to-stopped","reaper-reaps-endpoint-rows"]}},"frontierMetrics":[{"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/durable-withdrawal-cleanup-intent-v2.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["withdrawal-intent-durable-across-teardown","lease-expiry-fallback-explicit"]}},{"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/durable-withdrawal-cleanup-intent-v2.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["reaper-drives-status-to-stopped","reaper-reaps-endpoint-rows"]}}],"authoringContractVersion":1,"statement":"A failed-join withdrawal no longer relies on a pure in-memory reconcile queue that teardown destroys: either a withdrawal intent is persisted before teardown so a later run completes it, or lease-expiry is explicitly documented as the designed fallback (the choice recorded in a finding), and a status-column and endpoint-row reaper alongside the existing lease sweep removes the residual stale rows that today no writer ever drives to STOPPED. doneWhen: the test-receipt probe reads solve/evidence/durable-withdrawal-cleanup-intent-v2.receipt.json with outstanding 0 — withdrawal-intent-durability and stale-row-reaper receipts passing (deterministic red-on-revert evidence harness).","title":null,"class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."},{"id":"explicit-choice","statement":"Choose one and record it in a finding: persist a withdrawal intent before teardown (durable retry owner), OR explicitly document lease-expiry as the designed fallback. Do not leave DEFERRED silently meaning 'not applied' with no owner."},{"id":"reaper-scope","statement":"Any reaper must drive the status column to STOPPED and reap endpoint rows, complementing (not replacing) the leader's lease sweep and the active-node projection's stale-lease trim; leftovers must be stale rows, not live routing targets."},{"id":"red-on-revert","statement":"Each new regression test must fail when the durable-intent or reaper mechanism is reverted while the rest of the change remains."}],"verificationTemplates":[],"frontierIds":["withdrawal-intent-durability","stale-row-reaper"]}}
{"ts":"2026-08-05T18:52:56.891Z","type":"finding","frontier":"withdrawal-intent-durability","claim":"explicit-choice recorded: lease-expiry is the DESIGNED fallback, made durable-in-effect by a new leader-side stale-row reaper, rather than a new node-local withdrawal-intent journal. Rationale: (1) the joining node's only node-local durable file (rejoin hints) is fire-and-forget and post-hydration; a reliable pre-teardown intent journal would need a new durable file, a teardown drain, replay-at-startup, and idempotent reaping — a large blast radius for a narrow defect; (2) the reaper covers the residual rows regardless of WHY the withdrawal was lost (deferred mutation, destroyed in-memory queue, or process kill), while an intent journal only covers the clean-teardown case; (3) the reaper-scope constraint already demands the reaper, so the marginal value of the journal is only the teardown-to-lease-expiry window, which the joiner itself covers by retrying. Reaper design: leader-side, alongside sweepExpiredLeases in lease-service; targets nodes rows stuck in status=joining with no live ready lease and no live transport (the failed-join leftovers the withdrawal never drove to STOPPED), drives status to STOPPED and reaps their node_endpoints/service_endpoints rows, complementing (not replacing) the lease sweep's connection_state=DISCONNECTED write and the active-node projection's stale-lease trim.","kind":"design","evidence":"explore:ses_02cd45d8effeDnaUx4NhP900VY","rulesOut":null,"verification":null,"regressionClassification":null,"scopePressureClassification":null}
{"ts":"2026-08-05T18:58:04.962Z","type":"attempt","frontier":"withdrawal-intent-durability","rung":"observe","rungIndex":1,"prevRungIndex":0,"hypothesis":"Add the leader-side stranded failed-join row reaper alongside sweepExpiredLeases in lease-service: nodes rows stuck in status=joining with no live ready lease and no live transport are driven to status=stopped (guarded on the observed joining status) and their node_endpoints (inactive) / service_endpoints (unhealthy) rows are reaped, complementing the lease sweep's connection_state write and the active-node projection's stale-lease trim. Closes the failed-join withdrawal durability gap (deferred mutation / destroyed in-memory reconcile queue / process kill) without a new node-local intent journal — the explicit-choice Solver finding records lease-expiry-plus-reaper as the designed fallback. Red-on-revert verified (2 assertions fail on revert); evidence harness 4/4; 6 suites 218 assertions green.","changeRef":"diff:solve/changes/durable-withdrawal-cleanup-intent-v2/attempt-1.diff","metricBefore":null,"metricAfter":0,"metricDirection":"lower-is-better","invalidSample":false,"baselineAbsent":true,"done":true,"evidence":"solve/evidence/durable-withdrawal-cleanup-intent-v2.receipt.json","beforeEvidence":"solve/evidence/durable-withdrawal-cleanup-intent-v2.receipt.json","beforeEvidenceIdentity":{"path":"solve/evidence/durable-withdrawal-cleanup-intent-v2.receipt.json","resolvedPath":"/media/peter/4509da27-4751-4dee-b366-f3983d0777252/peter/projects/lagrange/solve/evidence/durable-withdrawal-cleanup-intent-v2.receipt.json","exists":false,"size":null,"mtimeMs":null,"sha256":null,"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/durable-withdrawal-cleanup-intent-v2.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["withdrawal-intent-durable-across-teardown","lease-expiry-fallback-explicit"]},"observedAt":"2026-08-05T18:51:51.004Z","fingerprint":"6b9adafb5196485354c88cbe7f6d53f91cd2a774cbf429387cabd41916675bda"},"beforeEvidenceFingerpr